---
import { REGISTRY_URL } from "@vinui/registry/config"

import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const registry = `${REGISTRY_URL}/react`

const tsconfig = `
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  }
}`

const tsconfigApp = `
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
    // ...keep the existing options
  }
}`

const viteConfig = `
import path from "node:path"
import tailwindcss from "@tailwindcss/vite"
import react from "@vitejs/plugin-react"
import { defineConfig } from "vite"

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      "@": path.resolve(__dirname, "./src"),
    },
  },
})`

const app = `
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogClose,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogFooter,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/dialog"

export default function App() {
  return (
    <main className="flex min-h-svh items-center justify-center gap-2">
      <Button>Save</Button>
      <Dialog>
        <DialogTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Delete…</DialogTrigger>
        <DialogContent>
          <DialogHeader>
            <DialogTitle>Delete project?</DialogTitle>
            <DialogDescription>This can't be undone.</DialogDescription>
          </DialogHeader>
          <DialogFooter>
            <DialogClose render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Cancel</DialogClose>
            <DialogClose render={<Button variant="destructive" />}>Delete</DialogClose>
          </DialogFooter>
        </DialogContent>
      </Dialog>
    </main>
  )
}`

const registries = `
{
  "registries": {
    "@vinui": "${registry}/{name}.json"
  }
}`
---

<DocsLayout title="Installation · React">
  <h1>Installation · React</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    vinui is a <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com">shadcn</a> style: you use the shadcn CLI and
    shadcn's component API, and get vinui's look. Components are copied into your project,
    built on <a href="https://base-ui.com">Base UI</a> and Tailwind CSS v4.
  </p>
  <p>
    Already using shadcn? Skip to <a href="#existing-project">Existing shadcn project</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="new-project">New project</h2>
  <p>
    This guide uses Vite. For other frameworks, set up Tailwind CSS v4 and the <code>@/</code> import alias as in <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/installation">shadcn's installation guide</a>, then
    continue from <a href="#init">Initialize vinui</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Create a project</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={`npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react-ts\ncd my-app`} />

  <h3>2. Add Tailwind CSS</h3>
  <CodeBlock code="npm install tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite" />
  <p>Replace everything in <code>src/index.css</code> with:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={`@import "tailwindcss";`} lang="css" file="src/index.css" />

  <h3>3. Set up the <code>@/</code> import alias</h3>
  <p>Add <code>paths</code> to both TypeScript configs:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tsconfig} lang="json" file="tsconfig.json" />
  <CodeBlock code={tsconfigApp} lang="jsonc" file="tsconfig.app.json" />
  <p>Then add the Tailwind plugin and the alias to Vite:</p>
  <CodeBlock code="npm install -D @types/node" />
  <CodeBlock code={viteConfig} lang="ts" file="vite.config.ts" />

  <h3 id="init">4. Initialize vinui</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={`npx shadcn@latest init ${registry}/init.json`} />
  <p>This writes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>components.json</code>, with the <code>@vinui</code> registry already configured</li>
    <li><code>src/lib/utils.ts</code>, shadcn's standard <code>cn()</code> helper</li>
    <li>vinui's theme (colors, radius, dark mode) into <code>src/index.css</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Nothing else: no shadcn theme, fonts or icon library.</p>

  <h3>5. Add components</h3>
  <CodeBlock code="npx shadcn@latest add @vinui/button @vinui/dialog" />
  <p>
    Each component lands in <code>src/components/ui/</code>, and its styles are added to <code>src/index.css</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Use them</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={app} lang="tsx" file="src/App.tsx" />
  <CodeBlock code="npm run dev" />

  <h2 id="existing-project">Existing shadcn project</h2>
  <p>vinui components can replace shadcn's one at a time.</p>
  <h3>1. Add the vinui registry</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={registries} lang="json" file="components.json" />
  <h3>2. Add components</h3>
  <CodeBlock code="npx shadcn@latest add @vinui/button" />
  <ul>
    <li>
      If you already have shadcn's version, the CLI asks before overwriting it. vinui uses
      the same props (<code>variant="outline"</code>, <code>size="sm"</code>, …), so your
      existing code keeps working.
    </li>
    <li>Your colors are kept; vinui only adds tokens your theme doesn't define yet.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>3. Switch to vinui's colors (optional)</h3>
  <CodeBlock code="npx shadcn@latest add @vinui/theme" />
  <p>
    This <strong>replaces</strong> the values of the tokens vinui defines
    (<code>--primary</code>, <code>--radius</code>, …) with vinui's. Tokens vinui doesn't
    define, such as <code>--card</code> or <code>--chart-1</code>, stay as they are.
  </p>

  <h2 id="dark-mode">Dark mode</h2>
  <p>
    Add the <code>dark</code> class to <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>; every component switches to
    the dark palette.
  </p>

  <h2 id="styling">Styling</h2>
  <p>
    Pass Tailwind classes with <code>className</code>; they override vinui's styles. For
    state-based styles, use data-attribute variants, for example <code>className="data-disabled:opacity-40"</code>. <code>className</code> takes a
    string; Base UI's function form isn't supported.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updating">Updating components</h2>
  <CodeBlock code="npx shadcn@latest add @vinui/button --overwrite" />
  <p>
    The CLI currently appends a component's nested <code>@media</code> and <code>@variant</code> rules again instead of replacing them. Before updating, delete the
    component's <code>@utility</code> blocks (for example <code>@utility btn</code> …) from <code>src/index.css</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
